"""Pure-Python font width metrics for summary layout estimation.

Replaces the former ReportLab ``stringWidth`` dependency. The per-character
advance-width tables below were extracted once from the Adobe standard-14
AFM metrics (via ReportLab's ``getFont(name).widths`` data) for Helvetica,
Helvetica-Bold, and Times-Roman, expressed in 1/1000ths of an em.

The summary pages are actually rendered by headless Chromium with the real
platform fonts (Avenir Next / Georgia on macOS, their fallbacks elsewhere),
which run slightly wider than the standard fonts measured here. Callers that
use these estimates to budget page heights should therefore inflate the
result with a safety factor (see ``SAFETY_FACTOR``) so estimates
over-predict and rendered pages never overflow.

Logical font names used by the summary estimator are mapped onto the three
measured tables:

    Summary-Avenir   -> Helvetica
    Summary-Georgia  -> Times-Roman
    Helvetica-Bold   -> Helvetica-Bold
"""

from typing import Dict, Mapping

#: Conservative multiplier applied by layout estimators on top of the raw
#: standard-font widths, because Chromium renders with wider system fonts
#: (Avenir Next, Georgia). Tuned against side-by-side Chromium renders.
SAFETY_FACTOR = 1.06

